IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `il-interpretation-time`
IMPORT domain

-- g2-validity.l4: section 8 of the Regulation of Engagement in Work on Refrigeration or Air-Conditioning
-- Systems Law 5785-2025, the period of validity of a licence, and the composition "the licence is in force on a day"
-- that the other groups consume (integration points IP1 and IP19).
--
-- IMPORTS.  This module imports only prelude, daydate, il-interpretation-time and domain.  Other g2- modules import this one;
-- no module of another group is imported anywhere in the group.
--
-- WHAT IS ENCODED.  s 8 states one rule with two parts: (i) a validity period of five years, or until 31 March of
-- "the fifth year from the year in which the licence was granted", whichever is earlier; (ii) a licence can be
-- renewed for further validity periods when the conditions of s 6 hold except s 6(a)(4).  Part (i) is here.  Part (ii)
-- needs the conditions of s 6 and is in g2-renewal.l4, which imports g2-conditions.
--
-- PERIODS.  The five years of limb 1 are a period of VALIDITY (kind V): IL s 10(b), "years after an event", the last
-- day counted inside the period.  31 March is a recurring calendar date (kind R), not a period.  Interpretation Law
-- s 10(c) is NOT applied to validity (the fleet's ruling 4); the alternative is callable below and tested.
-- ("IL s 10(c)" is the Interpretation Law's provision; the Law under encoding has a s 10(c) of its own, which is not
-- touched here.)
--
-- FORKS REGISTERED IN THIS MODULE (full text in FRAGMENT-G2.md section 2):
--   FV1 (trap T24)  which year is "the fifth year from the year in which the licence was granted":
--                   TAKEN year of grant + 5; alternative year of grant + 4.
--   FV2 (kind V)    IL s 10(c) on a period of validity: TAKEN not applied; alternative applied to the five year limb.
--   FV3 (P3)        which year is "the year in which the licence was granted" for a RENEWED licence: TAKEN each
--                   renewal begins a validity period counted from the renewal day; alternative each further period
--                   continues from the day after the previous one ends.
--   FV4             first day of validity: TAKEN the day of the grant; alternative the day after it (the module's
--                   "first day of a period counted from or after an event").
--   FV5             the register's recorded last day (which is how an extension under s 17(c) reaches this module):
--                   TAKEN it governs where there is one; alternative the Law alone governs.
--   FV6             the day a recorded revocation or suspension takes effect: TAKEN the day recorded; alternative
--                   the day after it.
--   FV7 (trap T25)  whether an extension of up to three months under s 17(c) can pass the 31 March limb:
--                   TAKEN it can; alternative it is capped.

§ `Section 8 — the period of validity of a licence`

-- The text of s 8, copied by script from inputs/law.wiki.
-- src:99 | {{ח:סעיף|8|תקופת תוקפו של רישיון וחידושו}}
-- src:100 | {{ח:ת}} תוקפו של רישיון יהיה לחמש שנים או עד 31 במרץ של השנה החמישית מהשנה שבה ניתן הרישיון, לפי המוקדם (להלן – תקופת תוקף), וניתן לחדשו לתקופות תוקף נוספות בהתקיים התנאים לפי {{ח:פנימי|סעיף 6|סעיף 6}}, למעט התנאי לפי {{ח:פנימי|סעיף 6|סעיף קטן (א)(4) של אותו סעיף}}.
@ref s 8, limb 1: five years from the day the licence was granted (src:100)
@desc The last day of the five-year limb of a validity period beginning on the given day (Interpretation Law s 10(b): the same-numbered day five years on, or the last day of a shorter month)
GIVEN `the day the validity period begins` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 8 — the last day of the five year limb of the validity period beginning on` `the day the validity period begins` MEANS
    `s 10(b) — the last day of a period of` 5 `years after an event on` `the day the validity period begins`

-- FV1.  "31 March of the fifth year from the year in which the licence was granted".  TAKEN: the fifth year FROM the
-- year of grant is the year of grant plus five.  Why: under year plus four the 31 March limb is always earlier than
-- five years (the five year anniversary falls in year plus five), so "whichever is earlier" would have no work to do
-- and limb 1 would be dead; under year plus five a grant on or before 31 March has the five year limb earlier and a
-- grant after it has the 31 March limb earlier, so both limbs of the Law's own words can govern.
@ref s 8, limb 2: until 31 March of the fifth year from the year in which the licence was granted (src:100)
GIVEN `the day the validity period begins` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 8 — the 31 March limb of the validity period beginning on` `the day the validity period begins` MEANS
    YMD (DATE_YEAR `the day the validity period begins` PLUS 5) 3 31

-- FV1, the alternative: the year of grant counted as the first year, so the fifth year is year of grant plus four.
@ref s 8, limb 2, the fifth year counted with the year of grant as the first (src:100)
GIVEN `the day the validity period begins` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 8 (the year of grant counted as the first year) — the 31 March limb of the validity period beginning on` `the day the validity period begins` MEANS
    YMD (DATE_YEAR `the day the validity period begins` PLUS 4) 3 31

@ref s 8, "whichever is earlier" (src:100)
@export The last day of the validity period of a licence granted (or renewed) on the given day: five years after that day, or 31 March of the fifth year from its year, whichever is earlier (Law s 8; the year of grant plus five reading)
GIVEN `the day the validity period begins` IS A DATE @desc The day the licence was granted, or the day a renewal began a further validity period
GIVETH A DATE
`s 8 — the last day of the validity period beginning on` `the day the validity period begins` MEANS
    IF   `s 8 — the 31 March limb of the validity period beginning on` `the day the validity period begins`
         AT MOST `s 8 — the last day of the five year limb of the validity period beginning on` `the day the validity period begins`
    THEN `s 8 — the 31 March limb of the validity period beginning on` `the day the validity period begins`
    ELSE `s 8 — the last day of the five year limb of the validity period beginning on` `the day the validity period begins`

@ref s 8, "whichever is earlier", with the year of grant counted as the first year (src:100)
GIVEN `the day the validity period begins` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 8 (the year of grant counted as the first year) — the last day of the validity period beginning on` `the day the validity period begins` MEANS
    IF   `s 8 (the year of grant counted as the first year) — the 31 March limb of the validity period beginning on` `the day the validity period begins`
         AT MOST `s 8 — the last day of the five year limb of the validity period beginning on` `the day the validity period begins`
    THEN `s 8 (the year of grant counted as the first year) — the 31 March limb of the validity period beginning on` `the day the validity period begins`
    ELSE `s 8 — the last day of the five year limb of the validity period beginning on` `the day the validity period begins`

-- FV2.  Interpretation Law s 10(c) on a period of validity.  TAKEN: not applied (a validity period is not a time for
-- doing something, and applying (c) would lengthen a licence by a rest day).  The alternative applies (c) to the five
-- year limb only: 31 March is a calendar date, not a period, so (c) has nothing to act on there.
@ref s 8, limb 1 with Interpretation Law s 10(c) applied (src:100)
GIVEN `the day the validity period begins` IS A DATE
      `the calendar of rest days` IS A `Calendar of rest days`
GIVETH A DATE
`s 8 (Interpretation Law s 10(c) applied to the five year limb) — the last day of the validity period beginning on` `the day the validity period begins` `, with` `the calendar of rest days` MEANS
    IF   `s 8 — the 31 March limb of the validity period beginning on` `the day the validity period begins`
         AT MOST `s 8 — the last day of the five year limb of the validity period beginning on` `the day the validity period begins`
    THEN `s 8 — the 31 March limb of the validity period beginning on` `the day the validity period begins`
    ELSE `s 10(c) — the last day of a period whose nominal last day is`
             (`s 8 — the last day of the five year limb of the validity period beginning on` `the day the validity period begins`)
             `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are`
             (`days of rest, recess or holiday listed in` (`the calendar of rest days`'s `days of rest, recess or holiday`))

§§ `Section 8 — the licence as the register records it`

-- A licence's validity period begins on the day it was granted or on a renewal day (FV3, below).
-- `renewed on` is oldest first; the latest day is taken by comparison, so an out-of-order list does no harm.
@ref s 8
GIVEN `the grant day` IS A DATE
      `the renewal days` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the latest of the grant day and the renewal days` `the grant day` `the renewal days` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the renewal days`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN `the grant day`
    WHEN r FOLLOWED BY more THEN
        `the latest of the grant day and the renewal days`
            (IF r AT LEAST `the grant day` THEN r ELSE `the grant day`)
            more

-- Named refusal: returned, never stored.
@ref s 9(a) read with s 8: the Law fixes no last day for a temporary licence
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the Law fixes no last day for a temporary licence and the register records none` MEANS
    REFUSE "the Law fixes no last day for a temporary licence (s 9(a) says only that its period may not exceed one year) and the register records none"

-- FV3.  TAKEN: each renewal begins a further validity period, counted from the renewal day under the same two limbs,
-- "the year in which the licence was granted" being read for a further period as the year it was granted that
-- period.  s 8 says "further validity periods" but not from when.  Renewals are taken to be made before the previous
-- period ran out; a renewal after a lapse is not provided for in the sources (FRAGMENT section 8).
@ref s 8, further validity periods on renewal (src:100)
GIVEN licence IS A Licence
GIVETH A DATE
`s 8 — the last day of validity of the licence, by the Law alone` licence MEANS
    IF   licence's `a temporary licence under section 9`
    THEN `the Law fixes no last day for a temporary licence and the register records none`
    ELSE `s 8 — the last day of the validity period beginning on`
             (`the latest of the grant day and the renewal days` (licence's `granted on`) (licence's `renewed on`))

-- FV3, the alternative: every further period continues from the day after the previous one ends.
@ref s 8
GIVEN `the number of renewals still to count` IS A NUMBER
      `the end of the previous period` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the end of the validity period after` `the number of renewals still to count` `renewals, continuing from` `the end of the previous period` MEANS
    IF   `the number of renewals still to count` AT MOST 0
    THEN `the end of the previous period`
    ELSE `the end of the validity period after` (`the number of renewals still to count` MINUS 1) `renewals, continuing from`
             (`s 8 — the last day of the validity period beginning on` (`s 10 — the first day of a period counted from or after an event on` `the end of the previous period`))

@ref s 8, further validity periods, each continuing from the end of the previous one (src:100)
GIVEN licence IS A Licence
GIVETH A DATE
`s 8 (each further period continues from the end of the previous one) — the last day of validity of the licence` licence MEANS
    IF   licence's `a temporary licence under section 9`
    THEN `the Law fixes no last day for a temporary licence and the register records none`
    ELSE `the end of the validity period after` (count (licence's `renewed on`)) `renewals, continuing from`
             (`s 8 — the last day of the validity period beginning on` (licence's `granted on`))

-- FV5.  The register (s 11(a)(1) records the licence's "period of validity") is how an extension under s 17(c)
-- reaches this module, so a recorded last day governs where there is one (integration point IP19).  The alternative,
-- the Law alone, is the function above.
@ref s 8 read with s 11(a)(1): the period of validity as the register records it (src:100)
@export The last day of validity of a licence: the last day the register records where there is one (which is how an extension under s 17(c) is carried), otherwise the last day the Law computes from the grant and renewal days (s 8)
GIVEN licence IS A Licence @desc The licence as the register records it
GIVETH A DATE
`s 8 — the last day of validity of the licence` licence MEANS
    CONSIDER licence's `validity ends on, as recorded`
    WHEN JUST recorded THEN recorded
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `s 8 — the last day of validity of the licence, by the Law alone` licence

-- FV4.  The licence is valid from the day it was granted, inclusive.  The alternative begins validity the day after
-- (the Interpretation Law's first day of a period counted from an event).
@ref s 8, the licence is valid for the validity period from the grant (src:100)
GIVEN licence IS A Licence
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 8 — the licence` licence `is within its period of validity on` day MEANS
        day AT LEAST licence's `granted on`
    AND day AT MOST `s 8 — the last day of validity of the licence` licence

@ref s 8, the licence is valid for the validity period from the grant (src:100)
GIVEN licence IS A Licence
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 8 (validity begins the day after the grant) — the licence` licence `is within its period of validity on` day MEANS
        day AT LEAST `s 10 — the first day of a period counted from or after an event on` (licence's `granted on`)
    AND day AT MOST `s 8 — the last day of validity of the licence` licence

-- FV5, the alternative: the Law alone.
@ref s 8 (src:100)
GIVEN licence IS A Licence
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 8 (the Law alone) — the licence` licence `is within its period of validity on` day MEANS
        day AT LEAST licence's `granted on`
    AND day AT MOST `s 8 — the last day of validity of the licence, by the Law alone` licence

-- FV3, the alternative, as a validity test.
@ref s 8 (src:100)
GIVEN licence IS A Licence
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 8 (each further period continues from the end of the previous one) — the licence` licence `is within its period of validity on` day MEANS
        day AT LEAST licence's `granted on`
    AND day AT MOST `s 8 (each further period continues from the end of the previous one) — the last day of validity of the licence` licence

§§ `Section 8 with section 10 — the licence is in force on a day`

-- FV6.  s 10 (group G1) revokes or suspends a licence; the register carries the result in `revoked on`,
-- `suspended from` and `suspended until` (domain.l4).  TAKEN: a licence is not in force from the day recorded as the
-- day of revocation, nor from the first day of a suspension until its last day (open-ended where no last day is
-- fixed).  The Law does not say when a decision under s 10 takes effect; the alternative takes effect the day after.
-- This module reads those three fields as facts; it does not decide whether s 10 was properly applied (G1).
-- Revocation: the licence is not in force from the day the decision takes effect.
@ref s 10 and s 11(a)(2): the register's record of revocation and suspension
GIVEN licence IS A Licence
      day IS A DATE
      effect IS A FUNCTION FROM DATE TO DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the register shows` licence `revoked on or before` day `, a decision taking effect from` effect MEANS
    CONSIDER licence's `revoked on`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST revoked THEN day AT LEAST effect revoked

-- Suspension: the licence is not in force from the first day of the suspension to its last day, or without end where
-- no last day is fixed (a suspension until final judgment, s 10(b)).
@ref s 10 and s 11(a)(2): the register's record of revocation and suspension
GIVEN licence IS A Licence
      day IS A DATE
      effect IS A FUNCTION FROM DATE TO DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the register shows` licence `suspended on` day `, a decision taking effect from` effect MEANS
    CONSIDER licence's `suspended from`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST began THEN
        IF   day AT LEAST effect began
        THEN CONSIDER licence's `suspended until`
             WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
             WHEN JUST until THEN day AT MOST until
        ELSE FALSE

@ref s 10 and s 11(a)(2): the register's record of revocation and suspension
GIVEN licence IS A Licence
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the register records the licence` licence `as revoked or suspended on` day MEANS
        `the register shows` licence `revoked on or before` day `, a decision taking effect from` (GIVEN d YIELD d)
    OR  `the register shows` licence `suspended on` day `, a decision taking effect from` (GIVEN d YIELD d)

@ref s 10 and s 11(a)(2): the register's record of revocation and suspension
GIVEN licence IS A Licence
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the register records the licence` licence `as revoked or suspended, taking effect the day after, on` day MEANS
        `the register shows` licence `revoked on or before` day `, a decision taking effect from` (GIVEN d YIELD `s 10 — the first day of a period counted from or after an event on` d)
    OR  `the register shows` licence `suspended on` day `, a decision taking effect from` (GIVEN d YIELD `s 10 — the first day of a period counted from or after an event on` d)

@ref s 8 with s 10 and s 11: the licence is in force on a day (integration point IP1) (src:100)
@export Whether a licence is in force on a day: within its period of validity (s 8, or the term the register records for a temporary licence under s 9) and not recorded as revoked or suspended (s 10)
GIVEN licence IS A Licence @desc The licence as the register records it
      day IS A DATE @desc The day asked about
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the licence is in force on` licence day MEANS
        `s 8 — the licence` licence `is within its period of validity on` day
    AND NOT `the register records the licence` licence `as revoked or suspended on` day

@ref s 10 and s 11(a)(2): the register's record of revocation and suspension
GIVEN licence IS A Licence
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the licence is in force on, a revocation or suspension taking effect the day after` licence day MEANS
        `s 8 — the licence` licence `is within its period of validity on` day
    AND NOT `the register records the licence` licence `as revoked or suspended, taking effect the day after, on` day

-- For the consumers (IP1): the kinds of licence among a person's licences that are in force on a day.
@ref s 8 with s 10 (integration point IP1)
@export The kinds of licence, among the given licences, that are in force on the given day
GIVEN day IS A DATE @desc The day asked about
      licences IS A LIST OF Licence @desc The licences the person holds or held, as the register records them
GIVETH A LIST OF `Licence kind`
`the licence kinds in force on the day` day licences MEANS
    map (GIVEN licence YIELD licence's `the kind of licence`)
        (filter (GIVEN licence YIELD `the licence is in force on` licence day) licences)

§§ `Section 17(c) read with section 8 — an extension of up to three months (trap T25)`

-- s 17(c) belongs to group G3, which decides whether the Registrar may extend; what this module owns is how the
-- extension meets s 8.  s 17(c) lets the Registrar "extend the validity period" of a licensee who has not completed the
-- training duty "by a period not exceeding three months".  A number of months after an event is IL s 10(b), the event
-- being the last day of validity; IL s 10(c) is not applied (validity, kind V).
-- FV7.  TAKEN: the extension runs on from the last day of validity even when that passes 31 March, because an
-- extension of the validity period that could not pass the end the Law gave would be no extension where the 31 March
-- limb governs.  Alternative: it is capped at the 31 March limb of the period it extends.
-- PART OF A MONTH (repaired 2026-10-14, defect D2, found by the independent test author).  s 17(c) allows an extension "not exceeding
-- three months", so an extension of half a month is within it.  The function below takes a WHOLE number of months, one to three, because
-- Interpretation Law s 10(b) fixes the last day of a period of months only for a whole number of months (it names "the same-numbered day"
-- some months on): a part of a month has no last day in the Law.  A part of a month, or any extension shorter than a month, is therefore
-- stated as the DAY the extension ends on, with `s 17(c) (to a stated day) — the last day of validity` ... `extended to` ... below, which
-- accepts any day after the last day of validity up to the last day of a period of three months after it.  Both forms refuse, with a
-- message that names the other form, outside what they take; neither guesses.
@ref s 17(c) read with s 8 (trap T25)
GIVEN `the last day of validity` IS A DATE
      `the extension in months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`s 17(c) — the last day of validity` `the last day of validity` `extended by` `the extension in months` `months` MEANS
    IF   `the extension in months` AT LEAST 1
         AND `the extension in months` AT MOST 3
         AND `s 10 — the number is a positive whole number of days, weeks, months or years` `the extension in months`
    THEN `s 10(b) — the last day of a period of` `the extension in months` `months after an event on` `the last day of validity`
    ELSE `s 17(c) allows an extension of up to three months; this form takes a whole number of months from one to three, and a part of a month is stated as the day the extension ends on with the function s 17(c) (to a stated day)`

@ref s 17(c) read with s 8 (trap T25)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`s 17(c) allows an extension of up to three months; this form takes a whole number of months from one to three, and a part of a month is stated as the day the extension ends on with the function s 17(c) (to a stated day)` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 17(c) allows an extension of up to three months; this form takes a whole number of months from one to three, and a part of a month is stated as the day the extension ends on with the function s 17(c) (to a stated day)"

-- The extension stated as the day it ends on.  s 17(c): "extend the validity period ... by a period not exceeding three months": the
-- extended last day is any day after the last day of validity that is not after the last day of a period of three months after it
-- (Interpretation Law s 10(b); s 10(c) is not applied, validity being kind V).  Refuses outside that range.
@ref s 17(c) read with s 8 (trap T25)
GIVEN `the last day of validity` IS A DATE
      `the day the extension ends` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 17(c) (to a stated day) — the last day of validity` `the last day of validity` `extended to` `the day the extension ends` MEANS
    IF   `the day the extension ends` GREATER THAN `the last day of validity`
         AND `the day the extension ends` AT MOST `s 10(b) — the last day of a period of` 3 `months after an event on` `the last day of validity`
    THEN `the day the extension ends`
    ELSE `s 17(c) allows an extension ending on a day after the last day of validity and not after the last day of three months from it; the day given is outside that range`

@ref s 17(c) read with s 8 (trap T25)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`s 17(c) allows an extension ending on a day after the last day of validity and not after the last day of three months from it; the day given is outside that range` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 17(c) allows an extension ending on a day after the last day of validity and not after the last day of three months from it; the day given is outside that range"

@ref s 17(c) read with s 8 (trap T25)
GIVEN `the last day of validity` IS A DATE
      `the extension in months` IS A NUMBER
      `the day the extended validity period began` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 17(c) (capped at the 31 March limb) — the last day of validity` `the last day of validity` `extended by` `the extension in months` `months, the period having begun on` `the day the extended validity period began` MEANS
    IF   `s 17(c) — the last day of validity` `the last day of validity` `extended by` `the extension in months` `months`
         AT MOST `s 8 — the 31 March limb of the validity period beginning on` `the day the extended validity period began`
    THEN `s 17(c) — the last day of validity` `the last day of validity` `extended by` `the extension in months` `months`
    ELSE `s 8 — the 31 March limb of the validity period beginning on` `the day the extended validity period began`
